      "attrs": {
        "text": "You are reviewing one task's implementation: spec compliance first, then code quality. Task-scoped gate, not a merge review.\n\n## What Was Requested\n\nRead the task brief: /Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-3-brief.md\n\nGlobal constraints from the spec that bind this task:\n- Config layering per architecture: defaults in code → YAML → env vars; `${VAR}` interpolation in YAML.\n- Defaults exactly: batch_max_events 500, batch_max_bytes 1 MiB, spool_max_bytes 512 MiB, flush_interval_s 5.0 (0 disables auto-flush thread), request_timeout_s 10.0, retry base 1.0/max 60.0/jitter true.\n- ProducerStoreConfig.backend is Literal[\"file\",\"db\"], default \"file\"; shipped config/msging.yaml must contain the producer_store stanza with file.path \"${TALIUM_DATA_DIR}/producers.json\" and empty db stanza.\n- A TODO(msging) marker in config.py noting migration to the future shared loader (per project TODO convention).\n- Commit messages never mention Claude/AI, no Co-Authored-By lines.\n\n## What the Implementer Claims They Built\n\nRead the implementer's report: /Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-3-report.md\n\n## Diff Under Review\n\n**Base:** 50f75ef\n**Head:** e39fd7e\n**Diff file:** /Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/review-50f75ef..e39fd7e.diff\n\nRead the diff file once — it is your view of the change. Do not re-run git commands; do not crawl the codebase; inspect outside the diff only for a concrete named risk, one focused check per risk, named in the report. Read-only review — do not mutate the working tree, index, HEAD, or branch state.\n\n## Do Not Trust the Report\nVerify claims against the diff; rationales never downgrade findings.\n\n## Tests\nImplementer ran tests with TDD evidence; do not re-run to confirm. Focused test only for a specific doubt. Warnings/noise in reported output are findings.\n\n## Part 1: Spec Compliance\nMissing / Extra / Misunderstood. ⚠️ for anything unverifiable from the diff.\n\n## Part 2: Code Quality\nQuality, tests (real behavior), structure (plan layout). Evidence: file:line for every finding/check.\n\nFinal message is the report itself: begin with the spec-compliance verdict; every line is a verdict, finding with file:line, or check you ran.\n\n## Calibration\nImportant = cannot be trusted until fixed. Coverage-breadth/polish = Minor. Plan-mandated defects are findings (labeled plan-mandated). Strengths first.\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Spec Compliance\n- ✅ | ❌ | ⚠️\n\n### Strengths\n### Issues\n#### Critical (Must Fix)\n#### Important (Should Fix)\n#### Minor (Nice to Have)\n\n### Assessment\n**Task quality:** [Approved | Needs fixes]\n**Reasoning:** [1-2 sentences]",
